    "Q10 and Q50 rankings are unstable between the 17-frame core and 33-frame sensitivity window; Q90 is more rank-stable in this four-stone sample.",
    "Several human-selected readable/crisp-tier frames have near-zero coarse adjacent-band separation in one pair, so coarse whole-band median contrast is not a sufficient proxy for visible tier legibility.",
    "Core Q50/Q90 separation is strongly rank-correlated with retained activation in this tiny sample and inner-middle Q50/Q90 is also strongly correlated with occupancy; incremental value is therefore unproven.",
    "The standardized challenger may change scale but cannot by itself recover spatial structure already averaged away by coarse band medians; it remains an experimental falsification test rather than a presumed fix."
